# Schema: Polkadot SDK PRDoc Schema (prdoc) v1.0.0
# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json

title: Collation protocol v4 with bounded segment advertisements

doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |
      This PR adds collation protocol v4 (`/collation/4`). A v4 collator advertises up to
      `MAX_SEGMENT_LEN` (32) candidates per scheduling parent and core in one `AdvertiseSegment`.
      There is no `Declare` and no `CollationSeconded` in v4. Collations are fetched over the new
      `/req_collation/3` protocol. v2/v3 validators get an `AdvertiseCollation` for the segment tip.

      v4 is the main collation protocol for collators and for validators running
      `--experimental-collator-protocol`, v3 and v2 are fallbacks. `PeerSetProtocolNames::new`
      picks the newest version now. Nodes running the old validator side have to pin v3 with
      `PeerSetProtocolNames::new_with_main_collation_version`, otherwise v4 advertisements from
      new collators are dropped. `/req_collation/3` has to be registered with the network, the
      receiver goes into `OverseerGenArgs::collation_req_v3_receiver`.

      - `CollationGenerationMessage::SubmitCollation` is replaced by `SubmitSegment`
        (`SubmitSegmentParams`, `SegmentCollation`), `CollatorProtocolMessage::DistributeCollation`
        by `DistributeSegment`. Segments are write-once per (scheduling parent, core).
      - `CollationResult::result_sender`, `CollationResult::into_inner`,
        `CollationSecondedSignal` and `TryFrom<&CollationSecondedSignal> for BlockAnnounceData`
        are removed.
      - `CandidateDescriptorVersion::Unknown` is now `Unknown(u8)`.
      - `PeerSet::get_main_version()` is removed. `Requests` and `Protocol` have a new
        `CollationFetchingV3` variant, `CollationProtocols` has a fourth type parameter for `V4`.
      - The lookahead collator builds one block per relay parent.

  - audience: Node Operator
    description: |
      No action needed. Validators only negotiate v4 with `--experimental-collator-protocol`
      (on by default on Kusama). There is no required upgrade order between validators and
      collators.

